cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the region-level conformal risk control
  framework it implements, please cite both the software and the paper.
title: >-
  ReCoRD: Region-Level Conformal Risk Control for Semantic Segmentation
  under Distribution Shift
abstract: >-
  Given a pretrained segmentation model, ReCoRD selects class-specific
  thresholds on held-out calibration data so that the fraction of missed
  ground-truth regions (connected components) of a designated critical class
  within an image, averaged over the images containing that class, is bounded
  by a chosen risk level, with finite-sample distribution-free validity.
  Deployment under distribution shift is handled by a two-tier scheme: exact
  recalibration from a small labeled target set, and a label-free
  importance-weighted variant over foundation-model embeddings carrying an a
  priori certificate that identifies vacuous calibration before any label is
  read. The repository contains the full pipeline, the committed splits and
  seeds, and the reporting scripts that produce every number, table and figure
  in the paper.
